    hook: "Every major contemplative tradition — Hindu Advaita Vedanta, Zen Buddhism, Taoism, Sufism, Christian mysticism — points toward the same insight: the separation between self and world, between observer and observed, between 'me' and 'everything else' is a mental construction, not an ultimate fact. What lies beneath this construction — what is aware before the division into self and world — is what these traditions call by different names: Brahman, Buddha-nature, the Tao, God, pure awareness. This is perhaps the most radical idea a human being can encounter — and it has the power to completely transform the experience of being alive.",
